      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/tests/gui/api-knowledge.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T10:30:30Z",
          "note": "api-knowledge.ts is clean, well-structured, and internally consistent. JSDoc comments on KnowledgeMoveBodySchema (lines 64-84) accurately describe the conditional-required pattern. The validationError() helper avoids code repetition cleanly. No observations beyond confirming the code is in good shape."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T10:30:30Z",
          "note": "tests/gui/api-knowledge.test.ts has a comment (line 2) saying 'Tests for WP-001: Knowledge Handler Foundations' but the file now contains test suites for WP-001, WP-004, WP-005 — the file-level comment is stale. Consider updating it to reflect the full scope, though this is cosmetic."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T10:30:30Z",
          "note": "tests/gui/api-knowledge.test.ts uses a local mirror function (parseKnowledgeIdMirror, findInsightByIdMirror) to test private module functions rather than exporting them. This pattern works but requires keeping mirrors in sync. Since parseKnowledgeId is now exported (line 103), the mirror approach in the test could be replaced by a direct import — reducing the sync burden."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-05-30T10:31:04Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-05-30T10:33:38Z",
      "duration_ms": 154000,
      "summary": [
        "Full Verification Stack executed against WP-005 (GUI API: Schemas and Handler Functions). Build: tsc --noEmit clean. All 83 api-knowledge tests pass. Full regression suite: 2700/2700 tests green. 6 additional QA edge-case stress tests all pass. All 6 WP-005 acceptance criteria verified through direct test execution of the dedicated 'WP-005 Acceptance Criteria' suite."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "83 api-knowledge tests + 2617 regression tests; 6 QA edge-case stress tests all pass",
        "tests_passed": 2700,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T10:33:38Z",
          "note": "AC-4 scope='project' rejection is enforced via Zod InsightScope enum at the schema parse boundary for handleUpdateKnowledge/handleMoveKnowledge, and via InsightScope.safeParse() check in handleDeleteKnowledge/handlePromoteKnowledge — consistent and correct across all four mutating handlers."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T10:33:38Z",
          "note": "EC-5 edge case: handleDeleteKnowledge with repository_name='../evil' does not validate the slug against PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX at the handler level (unlike KnowledgeMoveBodySchema which uses .regex(PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX)). However, the storage layer throws when the constructed path is not found — meaning path traversal attempts throw NOT_FOUND rather than silently succeeding. This is a defense-in-depth gap (no explicit regex rejection at the handler level for delete/promote), but the behavior is safe in practice. Low priority recommendation for the Security Auditor to assess."
